1868-5fb9-b847-dd44e4a77dc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-96744" :question/problem "Which of the following functions has the codomain $(-2,2]?$\n\n- $p:(-2,2]\\to (-2,2]$\n- $q:R\\to [-2,2)$\n- $r:[-2,2)\\to (-2,2]$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $(-2,2],$ the interval from $-2$ to $2$ (including $2$ but not including $-2$).\n\n- The codomain of $q$ is $[-2,2),$ the interval from $-2$ to $2$ (including $-2$ but not including $2$).\n\n- The codomain of $r$ is $(-2,2],$ the interval from $-2$ to $2$ (including $2$ but not including $-2$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-96744/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbac348b-629f-52a1-9bb3-0d3f8483ff44"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-96744"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104781/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "18c53033-2638-59e1-b3be-4dab028d240e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104781/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "8caf0aa7-91d8-5148-a790-ec43ff6e0e25" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104781/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "57372209-b4fc-57c3-bd68-b4d674865369" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104781/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "40aad76c-bc42-5740-91a7-abfd42184d90" :a